    <!-- ==================== PDF certificate (Phase 5) ====================
         The framing lines are drawn in a box at the TOP of the certificate,
         before any hash or verdict. research/06 §7 requires the document to state
         what it does not establish; BSA 2023 s.63 requires human certification,
         so this must never present itself as self-sufficient proof. -->
    <string name="certificate_action">Certificate</string>
    <string name="certificate_generating">Building certificate…</string>
    <string name="certificate_title">Reality Lock — Event Proof Certificate</string>
    <string name="certificate_saved">Certificate saved.</string>
    <string name="certificate_save_failed">Could not save the certificate: %1$s</string>
    <string name="certificate_framing_1">This certificate reports the result of recomputing a cryptographic proof package. It establishes that the media and metadata are unaltered since capture and were signed by one specific key held in the capturing device keystore.</string>
    <string name="certificate_framing_2">It does NOT prove that the depicted event was real, unstaged, or correctly described.</string>
    <string name="certificate_framing_3">It is NOT a standalone legal certificate. Under the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam 2023 s.63, electronic evidence requires certification by a person; this document is generated automatically and requires human countersignature to be produced as evidence.</string>
    <string name="certificate_framing_4">Location is shown to three decimal places (~100 m). The exact coordinate remains in the proof package.</string>

    <!-- Bystander notice, shown under the live preview whenever the camera is
         bound. research/06 §3.2 asks for an affordance aimed at people captured
         incidentally: under the DPDP Act 2023 a bystander whose face and
         location are recorded is plausibly a Data Principal too, and is the one
         party who never saw a consent screen. Deliberately not dismissible. -->
    <string name="capture_bystander_notice">This device is recording a tamper-evident record: photo, location and time.</string>

    <!-- ============ BSA 2023 s.63 statutory annexure (Phase 7) ============
         A SEPARATE document from the certificate above, and deliberately so.
         The certificate reports what this system computed. This is a DRAFT FORM
         whose load-bearing content is what a person adds to it.

         Every statement below is drawn from research/06 §1.2-§1.3, not
         paraphrased from memory: s.63(4) requires dual certification (device
         custodian + independent expert), the Schedule requires the hash value
         and algorithm, the certificate must originate from whoever CONTROLS the
         device, and it must speak to matters this system cannot know — that the
         device "was operating properly", that information was fed "in the
         ordinary course of activity", and chain-of-custody after the file leaves
         the phone.

         This is not legal advice and the app must never imply it is; research/06
         opens with that same caveat. -->
    <string name="annexure_action">s.63 annexure</string>
    <string name="annexure_generating">Building annexure…</string>
    <string name="annexure_title">Draft Technical Annexure — Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam 2023, s.63</string>
    <string name="annexure_saved">Draft annexure saved.</string>
    <string name="annexure_save_failed">Could not save the annexure: %1$s</string>
    <string name="annexure_draft_notice">DRAFT — NOT A CERTIFICATE. This document is generated automatically by software and has no legal force as produced. Under BSA 2023 s.63(4) a certificate must be signed by a natural person in a responsible position in relation to the device, and additionally by an independent expert. This annexure supplies the technical particulars such a certifier would reference; it does not, and cannot, certify anything itself.</string>

    <!-- Method of production. Describes what the software actually does, in the
         order it does it — not an idealised account. -->
    <string name="annexure_method_1">The image was captured by the Reality Lock application directly from the device camera. The application provides no path for importing an existing image from storage or the gallery.</string>
    <string name="annexure_method_2">Location, timestamp, motion-sensor and device metadata were recorded at the moment of capture and canonicalised using JSON Canonicalization Scheme (RFC 8785).</string>
    <string name="annexure_method_3">SHA-256 digests were computed over the image bytes and over the canonicalised metadata, and combined into a two-leaf Merkle root. This root is the hash value stated above.</string>
    <string name="annexure_method_4">The Merkle root was signed with an ECDSA P-256 key generated inside the device keystore and marked non-exportable, so the private key cannot be read out of the device by any application, including this one.</string>
    <string name="annexure_method_5">Where the device supports it, a hardware key-attestation certificate chain was recorded alongside the signature, evidencing that the signing key resides in the device secure hardware.</string>

    <!-- Matters the SIGNATORIES must attest to, because the system cannot.
         Each maps to a specific limitation identified in research/06 §1.3. -->
    <string name="annexure_attest_1">That the device was operating properly throughout the relevant period, in the sense required by the statute; the application records its own operation but cannot attest to the condition of the device as a whole.</string>
    <string name="annexure_attest_2">That the information was fed into the device in the ordinary course of activity.</string>
    <string name="annexure_attest_3">That the signatory occupies a responsible position in relation to the operation of the device or the management of the relevant activities.</string>
    <string name="annexure_attest_4">Chain of custody after the record left the device — how it was transferred, stored, and produced — none of which the application observes.</string>
    <string name="annexure_attest_5">That the scene depicted is what it is asserted to be. The cryptographic record establishes that the image is unaltered since capture; it says nothing about whether the subject was staged, or about the truth of any description attached to it.</string>

    <string name="annexure_signatory_custodian_role">1. Person in charge of the device (device custodian)</string>
    <string name="annexure_signatory_custodian_basis">Required by BSA 2023 s.63(4). Courts require the certificate to originate from whoever controls the device, not from a third-party application vendor.</string>
    <string name="annexure_signatory_expert_role">2. Independent expert</string>
    <string name="annexure_signatory_expert_basis">Required by BSA 2023 s.63(4), which introduced mandatory dual certification. This signatory must be independent of the device custodian.</string>

